From: Kyvenza <support@kyvenza.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 23:20:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hvf: arm: drop data-abort writes without ISV instead of
 asserting

A store without a valid instruction syndrome (STP, SIMD, SVE) to an
address nothing decodes hit assert(isv) and took the VM down. Windows
on a virtio-gpu with hostmem does this late in shutdown: it clears
memory decoding on the device, which removes the 8 GiB hostmem BAR,
and a user process then stores through a mapping of a blob it has not
torn down yet (traced: BAR removed 0.7 ms before the first such store;
166 of them in one shutdown, 3 aborts in a day of testing).

Drop such writes and step over the instruction. That is what the
emulated path already does for a write nothing decodes, and what the
hardware does for a write to a disabled BAR. Injecting a synchronous
external abort instead, as KVM does for KVM_EXIT_ARM_NISV, made that
Windows shutdown hang, so it is only kept for reads, where there is no
way to know the destination register.
---
 target/arm/hvf/hvf.c | 38 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/target/arm/hvf/hvf.c b/target/arm/hvf/hvf.c
index 6df4c221215..8d6767cfaf1 100644
--- a/target/arm/hvf/hvf.c
+++ b/target/arm/hvf/hvf.c
@@ -2467,10 +2467,42 @@ static int hvf_handle_exception(CPUState *cpu, hv_vcpu_exit_exception_t *excp)
         assert(!s1ptw);
 
         /*
-         * TODO: ISV will be 0 for SIMD or SVE accesses.
-         * Inject the exception into the guest.
+         * ISV is 0 for SIMD, SVE and load/store-pair accesses, so there is no
+         * register to emulate the MMIO access with. Don't take the whole VM
+         * down for it: Windows stores through a stale user mapping of an
+         * unmapped hostmem blob late in shutdown.
+         *
+         * A write is dropped, which is what the emulated path above does for
+         * a write nothing decodes. Injecting an external abort for it instead
+         * (what KVM does for KVM_EXIT_ARM_NISV) hung that Windows shutdown.
+         * A read needs a destination register we cannot know, so it still
+         * gets the external abort.
          */
-        assert(isv);
+        if (!isv && iswrite) {
+            /* no cpu_synchronize_state() here: advance_pc writes the vCPU PC directly */
+            qemu_log_mask(LOG_GUEST_ERROR,
+                          "hvf: dropping a write without ISV at IPA 0x%" PRIx64
+                          " (va 0x%" PRIx64 ")\n", ipa,
+                          (uint64_t)excp->virtual_address);
+            advance_pc = true;
+            break;
+        }
+        if (!isv) {
+            int target_el;
+
+            cpu_synchronize_state(cpu);
+            target_el = MAX(arm_current_el(env), 1);
+            qemu_log_mask(LOG_GUEST_ERROR,
+                          "hvf: data abort without ISV at IPA 0x%" PRIx64
+                          " (pc 0x%" PRIx64 "), injecting an external abort\n",
+                          ipa, env->pc);
+            env->exception.vaddress = excp->virtual_address;
+            hvf_raise_exception(cpu, EXCP_DATA_ABORT,
+                                syn_data_abort_no_iss(arm_current_el(env) == target_el,
+                                                      0, 1, 0, 0, iswrite, 0x10),
+                                target_el);
+            break;
+        }
 
         /*
          * Emulate MMIO.
